{"name":"White Hot Chocolate","hex":"#ead8bb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"hot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Hote."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to heat and conditions which produce it.\n Having or giving off a high temperature.","Having or giving off a high temperature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot"},{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot chocolate, also known as hot cocoa or drinking chocolate, is a heated drink consisting of shaved or melted chocolate or cocoa powder, and heated milk or water. It usually contains a sweetener, such as sugar, and is often garnished with whipped cream or marshmallows or both. Hot chocolate made with melted chocolate is characterized by less sweetness and a thicker consistency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg/330px-After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_chocolate"},{"title":"Hot Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Chocolate are a British soul band formed by Errol Brown and Tony Wilson. The group had at least one hit song every year on the UK Singles Chart from 1970 to 1984."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/The_Hot_Chocolate.jpg/330px-The_Hot_Chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Chocolate"},{"title":"White hot","blocks":[{"text":"The white hot is a variation on the hot dog found primarily in the Rochester, New York area, as well as other parts of Western New York and Central New York. It is composed of a combination of uncured and unsmoked pork, beef, and veal; the lack of smoking or curing allows the meat to retain a naturally white color. White hots usually contain mustard and other spices, and often include a dairy component such as nonfat dry milk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/White_hot_dog_exterior_detail.JPG/330px-White_hot_dog_exterior_detail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_hot"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg/250px-Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c